cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "Context Re-projection: rebuilding an agent's context from durable state versus letting a transcript accumulate"
abstract: >-
  A controlled study of two context strategies for long-horizon coding agents.
  One arm re-projects the prompt from durable state at every task boundary; the
  control lets the transcript accumulate and truncates from the front at a
  ceiling. Includes the harness, the arms, the task sets, the evaluation code,
  and the raw run data for every cell.
